+      .quote-strip { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
+      .quote { min-height: auto; }
+      .future-box { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: 21px; }
+      .big-arrow { width: 52px; height: 52px; font-size: 25px; }
+    }
+    @media (max-width: 420px) {
+      .wrap { width: calc(100% - 26px); }
+      .brand { font-size: 12px; }
+      .brand-mark { width: 30px; height: 30px; }
+      .toggle { padding: 7px 9px; font-size: 10px; }
+      h1 { font-size: clamp(46px, 14vw, 58px); }
+      .hero-copy { font-size: 15px; }
+      .crew-grid { gap: 11px; }
+      .card-inner { padding: 10px; }
+      .card-meta { font-size: 8px; }
+      .card h3 { font-size: 20px; }
+      .detail { font-size: 10px; }
+      .fact { font-size: 9px; }
+      .footer-row { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; }
+    }
+    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { *, *::before, *::after { scroll-behavior: auto !important; transition-duration: .01ms !important; } }
+  </style>
+</head>
+<body>
+  <header class="wrap topbar">
+    <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Group 14 home"><span class="brand-mark">G14</span><span>HUMANS IN THE LOOP</span></a>
+    <nav class="topnav" aria-label="Main navigation">
+      <a href="#crew">The crew</a>
+      <a href="#ai">Our AI take</a>
+      <button class="toggle" id="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false">☾ Night mode</button>
+    </nav>
+  </header>
+
+  <main id="top">
+    <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
+      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Paderborn University · Group 14</div>
+      <h1 id="hero-title">We build things.<br>We <span>double-check</span><br>the things.</h1>
+      <p class="hero-copy">Five computer scientists, one shared instinct: let the tools help, keep the humans responsible. Meet the people behind the prompts, pull requests and 3 a.m. hot takes.</p>
+      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="cta" href="#crew">Meet your engineering team ↘</a><span class="hero-note">CURRENT STATUS: curious / caffeinated / reviewing</span></div>
+    </section>
+
+    <div class="ticker" aria-label="Team motto"><div class="ticker-inner"><span>BUILD</span><b>✳</b><span>TEST</span><b>✳</b><span>READ THE CODE</span><b>✳</b><span>BUILD</span><b>✳</b><span>TEST</span><b>✳</b><span>READ THE CODE</span><b>✳</b><span>BUILD</span><b>✳</b><span>TEST</span><b>✳</b><span>READ THE CODE</span></div></div>
+
+    <section class="wrap" id="crew" aria-labelledby="crew-title">
+      <div class="section-head">
+        <div><p class="kicker">01 / The humans</p><h2 id="crew-title">Meet the crew.</h2></div>
+        <p class="section-note">Different routes into computer science. The same excellent habit of asking “but did we test it?”</p>
+      </div>
+      <div class="crew-grid">
+        <article class="card">
+          <img class="portrait" src="{{image:aryan.jpg}}" alt="Portrait of Aryan">
+          <div class="card-inner"><div class="card-meta"><span>01 / backend & agents</span><span>● online</span></div><h3>Aryan</h3>
+            <p class="detail"><strong>STUDY / WORK</strong><br>M.Sc. Computer Science at Paderborn; B.Sc. Computer Science from Chandigarh University. Former Associate Software Engineer at Toddle, plus a research internship at NYCU in Taiwan.</p>
+            <p class="detail"><strong>INTO</strong><br>Agentic AI, backend systems, learning German one Artikel at a time.</p>
+            <p class="fact"><b>FUN FACT →</b> His German is A2, so he and his coding agent are both still learning to follow instructions.</p>
+          </div>
+        </article>
+        <article class="card">
+          <img class="portrait" src="{{image:cemon.jpg}}" alt="Portrait of Cemon">
+          <div class="card-inner"><div class="card-meta"><span>02 / the next episode</span><span>● online</span></div><h3>Cemon</h3>
+            <p class="detail"><strong>STUDY / WORK</strong><br>M.Sc. Computer Science at Paderborn; B.E. in Computer Science and Engineering from Dayananda Sagar College of Engineering, Bangalore. 3.5 years as a software developer.</p>
+            <p class="detail"><strong>INTO</strong><br>Music and AI concepts.</p>
+            <p class="fact"><b>FUN FACT →</b> One episode can become 3 a.m. somehow. The autoplay button knows.</p>
+          </div>
+        </article>
+        <article class="card">
+          <img class="portrait" src="{{image:rachana.jpg}}" alt="Portrait of Rachana">
+          <div class="card-inner"><div class="card-meta"><span>03 / tabs multiply</span><span>● online</span></div><h3>Rachana</h3>
+            <p class="detail"><strong>STUDY / WORK</strong><br>M.Sc. Computer Science at Paderborn; B.E. in Artificial Intelligence and Data Science from East West Institute of Technology, Bangalore.</p>
+            <p class="detail"><strong>INTO</strong><br>Machine learning, data science, AI-powered apps, reading, music and cooking.</p>
+            <p class="fact"><b>FUN FACT →</b> Opens the laptop for one quick thing; emerges with 15 tabs and a different task.</p>
+          </div>
+        </article>
+        <article class="card">
+          <img class="portrait" src="{{image:shrividya.jpg}}" alt="Portrait of Shrividya">
+          <div class="card-inner"><div class="card-meta"><span>04 / passes the ball</span><span>● online</span></div><h3>Shrividya</h3>
+            <p class="detail"><strong>STUDY / WORK</strong><br>M.Sc. Computer Science at Paderborn; B.E. in Information Science and Engineering from Global Academy of Technology, Bengaluru. Cybersecurity internships in cloud security, DevSecOps and security automation.</p>
+            <p class="detail"><strong>INTO</strong><br>Sketching, basketball, dancing, new places and cultures, and trying new technologies.</p>
+            <p class="fact"><b>FUN FACT →</b> Basketball taught her teamwork—even when nobody wants to pass the ball.</p>
+          </div>
+        </article>
+        <article class="card">
+          <img class="portrait" src="{{image:srajan.jpg}}" alt="Portrait of Srajan">
+          <div class="card-inner"><div class="card-meta"><span>05 / cloud & football</span><span>● online</span></div><h3>Srajan</h3>
+            <p class="detail"><strong>STUDY / WORK</strong><br>M.Sc. Computer Science at Paderborn; B.E. in Computer Science and Engineering from New Horizon College of Engineering, Bangalore. Former Cloud Engineer at AWS; now a Werkstudent data scientist at Uniper.</p>
+            <p class="detail"><strong>INTO</strong><br>Football, video games and cloud architecture.</p>
+            <p class="fact"><b>FUN FACT →</b> Can watch a 0–0 draw for 90 minutes and call it tactically fascinating.</p>
+          </div>
+        </article>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="ai-section" id="ai" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
+      <div class="wrap">
+        <div class="section-head">
+          <div><p class="kicker">02 / The group chat, summarized</p><h2 id="ai-title">Our shared view on AI and the future of software engineering</h2></div>
+          <p class="section-note">Five perspectives, one strong review culture. Nobody gave the bot production access.</p>
+        </div>
+        <div class="ai-board">
+          <article class="ai-panel agree"><h3>Where we agree / human judgment stays on call</h3>
+            <ul>
+              <li>AI makes coding faster: useful for boilerplate, first drafts, tests, refactoring, finding bugs and exploring possible solutions.</li>
+              <li>Its output is a draft, not a verdict. It can invent APIs, make mistakes that are easy to miss, or offer a perfectly formatted guess.</li>
+              <li>Developers remain responsible for testing, reviewing and understanding the result. Human judgment is what checks that it is correct, reliable and solves the real problem.</li>
+              <li>Over the next 5–10 years, we expect more time spent specifying, planning, guiding agents and verifying their work—and less time writing every line from scratch.</li>
+            </ul>
+          </article>
+          <article class="ai-panel differ"><h3>Where the emphasis differs / same destination, different route</h3>
+            <ul>
+              <li>Aryan calls out system design, clear specifications, testing and observability; Rachana stresses problem-solving and keeping coding knowledge sharp.</li>
+              <li>Cemon puts clear requirements and prompt engineering front and center as AI takes on most coding tasks.</li>
+              <li>Shrividya imagines agents handling bigger jobs—including testing and bug fixes—while fundamentals help us catch their mistakes.</li>
+              <li>Srajan adds explainability to the core skills: if we cannot explain an AI's choice, it is still a guess.</li>
+            </ul>
+          </article>
+        </div>
+        <div class="quote-strip" aria-label="Team hot takes">
+          <blockquote class="quote">“AI won't replace developers who write tests. It will replace the ones who never read the code it writes.”<cite>— Aryan / hot take</cite></blockquote>
+          <blockquote class="quote">“AI can write a thousand lines of code in seconds, but finding the one tiny mistake that breaks everything is a different story.”<cite>— Rachana / hot take</cite></blockquote>
+          <blockquote class="quote">“An AI you can’t explain is just a very expensive guess with good formatting.”<cite>— Srajan / hot take</cite></blockquote>
+        </div>
+        <div class="quote-strip">
+          <blockquote class="quote">“Software engineers spend time and take responsibility for testing the code which they didn't write.”<cite>— Cemon / hot take</cite></blockquote>
+          <blockquote class="quote">“AI can write the code, but it cannot take responsibility when the system breaks at 3 AM!”<cite>— Shrividya / hot take</cite></blockquote>
+          <blockquote class="quote">TEAM RULE: ship the assist, keep the accountability.<cite>— Group 14 / release checklist</cite></blockquote>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <section class="future wrap" aria-label="Team outlook">
+      <div class="future-box">
+        <div><p class="kicker">Forecast / 5–10 years</p><h2>Less typing. More thinking. Still read the diff.</h2><p>Our shared bet: software engineers will spend more time shaping the problem, checking the system and making decisions. AI may become a normal teammate; knowing the basics is how we know when that teammate is confidently wrong.</p></div>
+        <div class="big-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+  </main>
+
+  <footer><div class="wrap footer-row"><span><strong>GROUP 14</strong> · built with human judgment (and a few helpful tools)</span><span>NO CDN · NO MAGIC FONTS · ALL HUMANS</span></div></footer>
+  <script>
+    const themeToggle = document.getElementById('theme-toggle');
+    const savedTheme = localStorage.getItem('group14-theme');
+    if (savedTheme === 'night') document.body.classList.add('night');
+    function syncThemeButton() {
+      const night = document.body.classList.contains('night');
+      themeToggle.textContent = night ? '☀ Day mode' : '☾ Night mode';
+      themeToggle.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(night));
+    }
+    syncThemeButton();
+    themeToggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
+      document.body.classList.toggle('night');
+      const night = document.body.classList.contains('night');
+      localStorage.setItem('group14-theme', night ? 'night' : 'day');
+      syncThemeButton();
+    });
+  </script>
+</body>
+</html>

